g weakness and  at the time being you want to kind of  hold back this deep to pawn if for  instance black were to try to bring his  pawn to d4 if he were to capture you  know from here White has the option of  just bringing this piece up kind of  waiting to see where this deep hunt  wants to go and then if black does  decide to capture then white can  recapture here but you don't want to  immediately move this this piece up  let's say we were just to move this  piece up here and then when they capture  then you recapture and then you don't  have you kind of have this F pawn hang  in there and then you have kind of a  weakness here so just a few tidbits to  kind of look at when you are playing the  game we'll go back to this position here  with the bishop on b2 and then from here  you'll just normally see black Castle  kingside so from here both sides are  gonna have you know a great game  obviously Black's trying to control the  light squares here and White's trying to  control the dark squares here so these  are some of the common things you want  to look for in the game if you see  something you know fishy that you're  like hey wait a minute just go ahead and  take and analyze the position see what  the other side is trying to do and play  from there the birds opening is not very  common so you're probably going to see  some pretty uncommon moves so just play  around with it  try to get better hope you guys enjoyed  if you haven't subscribed to go ahead  and subscribe and I'll see you guys next  video thanks for watching

